== the baseline is the file itself, and cannot carry an overlay ==
action=refused — the baseline is the file itself — make a branch to experiment on
== so: a branch at the top section, then an overlay below it ==
action=branched br-1 Robust
action=overlay-began on sec-2
  an overlay opens as a COPY of what is there:
    |function score(t)
    |  return t * 100
    |end function
== typing into it ==
action=overlay-saved sec-2
branch kind: code
== and it is VISIBLY MARKED experimental (§9.2) ==
    Baseline
  * Robust [experimental: 1 section(s)]
    +
  branch: Robust [experimental: 1 section(s)]
== the branch sees different source; the DOCUMENT does not ==
overlaid=true applied=sec-2
document still says:
    |threshold = 0.5
    |
    |function score(t)
    |  return t * 100
    |end function
    |
    |print "score is " + score(threshold)
    |
== compare ==
Robust against the file:
  sec-2:
    1 line(s) unchanged above
    -   return t * 100
    +   if t < 0 then
    +     return 0
    +   end if
    +   return t * 1000
    1 line(s) unchanged below
== running the branch runs the OVERLAY ==
   exec: run: finished [sec-3] — exit 0
target=<score is 500
>
== and the canonical file on disk was never touched ==
  size unchanged:  true
  bytes unchanged: true
== an overlay survives a close and a relaunch ==
edits restored: 1
  br-1 / sec-2
branches restored: 1
== the baseline still runs the file ==
action=baseline
   exec: run: finished [sec-3] — exit 0
target=<score is 50
>
